1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,550
Most goalkeepers stop the ball with their hands.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,650
This one… used his heels.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,550
Upside down.

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,850
September 6, 1995. Wembley.

5
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,450
England against Colombia.

6
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,350
Just a friendly. What could possibly go wrong?

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,850
In goal for Colombia: René Higuita.

8
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,450
His nickname? El Loco. The madman.

9
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,950
Jamie Redknapp tries a lob from 30 yards.

10
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,650
A soft, easy ball. Any keeper would just catch it.

11
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:25,550
Not Higuita.

12
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,250
He dives forward… flips his legs over his head…

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,650
…and kicks it away with his heels.

14
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:33,950
20,000 people at Wembley had never seen anything like it.

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,750
And the funniest part? The flag was already up for offside.

16
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,550
He didn’t even need to save it.

17
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:44,050
It wasn’t luck, either. He later said he’d practised it… all through the warm-up.

18
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,850
The match ended nil-nil. Nobody remembers the score.

19
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,750
Would you try this in goal?

20
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,150
Tell me in the comments.
